WEBVTT

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:14.010
Huh?

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:20.370
So this is where you used to live.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:27.250
I also lived here in Kamakura in my younger days.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:31.130
What were you called back when you were in middle school? {she uses "obaachan" here but I can't think of a good way to render it in English. D:} {How's "ma'am?"}

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.590
We just stuck to using surnames, so I was Godai.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.080
Godai?

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.120
Godai Kaoruko...

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:43.890
Wait, the youngest ever winner of the National Karate Championships, Godai Kaoruko?

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.270
You're remarkably well-informed, considering how long ago it was.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.290
Whaaaaaat?!

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:51.490
No way!

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:52.010
{OP}

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:55.200
HeartCatch

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.660
Precure!

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:00.240
HeartCatch Precure!

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:03.210
Now, all together

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:05.710
HeartCatch Precure!

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.720
Let's make our flowers bloom

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.310
Within each of our chests,

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.980
they begin to sprout

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:20.650
The seeds of the heart

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:21.930
are growing

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:24.560
bit by bit

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:25.230
Red,

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:25.850
white

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.150
and yellow

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:29.900
It's because these blooming buds are

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:31.360
all varied colors

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:32.810
that they

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:34.990
shine so brightly!

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:40.280
That smile that you've nurtured

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.790
with such care

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:45.490
will never wither

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:49.130
HeartCatch Precure!

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:52.000
Now, all together

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.460
HeartCatch Precure!

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:57.130
Let's make our flowers bloom!

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:02.050
They're always right by our sides

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:02.880
So together

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:06.680
let's make those pretty flowers of our heart

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.680
bloom even more!

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:11.180
HeartCatch

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.690
Precure!

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:21.540
You lived around here?

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:25.950
We lived a little further up in the mountains, but I remember coming here to shop a lot.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.450
Hanasaki?!

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:30.710
Oh! Mitsuru!

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:32.750
It's been a while, hasn't it?

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:34.690
You're back, then?

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:38.960
Oh, no. My friends and I are just 
here to visit during the Bon Festival.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:40.190
Afternoon!

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.640
Nice to meet you. I'm Myoudouin Itsuki.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.630
You're one of Hanasaki's friends, then?!

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:49.080
What of it?

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:52.900
Um, this is my childhood friend, Nakano Mitsuru.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:54.360
Nice to meet ya.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:56.320
L-Likewise...

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.040
You seem to be doing well, Mitsuru.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.860
How goes your kendo training?

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:04.410
I've been training day in and day out to get ready for the tournament. {Added the 'and.'}

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:07.580
I don't have the time to go waltzing 
about with girls whenever I feel like it.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:10.160
Aha, I see the problem.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:15.090
That's sweet. You've made me remember my first love.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:17.060
Your first love?

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:25.100
Grandpa was a Hottie<i>?!</i>

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:25.100
Grandpa was a Hottie<i>?!</i>

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.940
I can't go on any longer!

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.770
Erika, that's pathetic!

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:38.490
I like to think I keep myself in pretty good shape, {lit: "good at physical activity". Feel free to find a more accurate balance if you can think of one. D:} {Added the 'pretty' modifier, let's call it good.}

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:41.860
but just climbing these mountain paths is so boring!

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.530
Let us go!

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.870
Look how well Grandma's doing compared to you!

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.910
All right, all right! I get it!

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:56.620
By the way, just what is your
 relationship with that Mitsuru kid?

00:03:56.620 --> 00:04:00.790
My relationship? We're childhood friends, that's all.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.510
Come on, tell us a bit more than that.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.300
Sure, I guess.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:14.690
Since he was young, Mitsuru's always been
 obsessed by kendo and trained almost constantly.

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:18.360
I was always quiet and rather reserved.{It's funny, the Japanese for "quiet" as in the personality trait is literally just "adult-like". This is why Japan sucks :V}

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:23.530
What?!

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:29.870
<i>But whenever I got into trouble, Mitsuru would always appear to save me.</i>

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:34.410
Hmph!

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.200
Are you all right?!

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:52.380
Even in junior high, Mitsuru always seemed to appear out of nowhere to help me.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.940
Then, once we'd decided we were going to move to Kibougahana,

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:01.360
I wanted to thank Mitsuru for all the kindness he'd shown me. {Removed 'before then' at the end of the line - not needed for English parsing.}

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:08.620
Mitsuru!

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:18.360
But you never managed to see him?

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.410
That's right. {Extend the timing on this a little, please.}

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:22.170
He seems like a nice kid.

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:24.640
But I wonder why he dislikes me so much.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:25.760
Yeah, I'm not sure either.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.640
You really don't get it?

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:28.620
Huh?

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.300
I really don't.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.280
Me neither.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:32.430
I don't know either!

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:36.150
Hanasaki

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:43.460
It's amazing how quickly houses fall
 into decay when nobody's living there. {no-one -> nobody}

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:46.700
This house has a lot of memories for your family, right, Tsubomi?

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:49.910
Yeah! I was born and raised here, after all!

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.870
Ow, that hurt...

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:04.840
That's...

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:09.300
Whoa! I recognize that hot guy!

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.890
What's the matter?

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:11.800
Whoa!

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:14.310
Wow, that sure takes me back.

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:17.940
Is this your first time seeing a photo of Sora?

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:18.990
Yeah, it is!

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:21.560
So he's your grandpa?!

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:24.360
It's kinda strange, though.

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:26.530
Whenever I find myself in trouble,

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:30.370
a guy who is the spitting image of 
this photo always comes to save me!

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:36.900
If it's all right, could you please tell us more about Grandpa? {Capitalized 'grandpa.'}

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:38.020
Yeah!

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:40.500
Like how you met, and when you first started going out!

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.460
It's an old, old story.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.250
Please tell us!

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:54.340
It all began when I was doing some secluded training in the mountains to prepare myself for the tournament.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:10.420
But I always felt so lonely, sleeping there alone at night.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:12.700
I couldn't take it any longer, so I decided to head back.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:27.830
All around that little mountain hut, my 
favorite flower, lavender, was blooming.

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:42.520
Hi there.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:43.700
Huh?

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:45.810
Please come in.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:48.390
I don't want to disturb your playing.

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:51.470
I enjoy performing more when there's an audience.

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:53.610
So please, come in.

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:56.220
Yessir.

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:58.080
I mean, um, right...

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:01.580
Oh, just a moment. I'll get you some lavender tea. {Removed 'I have just the thing,' as this was WAY TOO MANY WORDS for such a short line (and according to Tiffany, is still close to what he actually says in moon, anyhow)}

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:57.300
You live in this mountain cottage all by yourself, Sora? {Original: "You mean to say you live in this little mountain cottage all by yourself, Sora?" I cut it down a bit because, again, too much :wordswordswords: for the timeframe, and she doesn't seem to be being that elaborate.}

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:58.500
Yes.

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:03.620
Nature has blessed this place well, and as such I'm able to live a self-sufficient lifestyle here.

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:05.730
Aren't you lonely out here on your own?

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:08.720
Of course I am.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:13.840
But the trees, plants, and leaves 
provide me most excellent company. {Added comma after 'plants.'}

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:17.200
Actually, I do happen to have something rather special. {Removed 'now I think of it' and changed 'Ah' to 'Actually.' Did you pick this translation up again at line 130ish after a break? It seems like the same issue keeps cropping up with his dialogue and I've never seen it from you before.}

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:21.450
A music box I made.

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:24.160
If ever you should feel lonely, then just listen to its melody. {Removed apostrophe from 'its.' You don't want 'it is' in there.}

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:27.600
Thank you...

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:38.070
And that was how I met Sora,

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:40.290
and how I found my first love.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:42.620
That's beautiful!

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:45.920
And after that, you went on to 
win the karate championships?

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:46.770
I did.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:50.650
I managed to continue my training, thanks to that music box.

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:56.380
After winning, I went on to study
 botany with the same enthusiasm,

00:09:57.390 --> 00:09:59.830
and I became closer and closer to Sora.

00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:03.900
What happened then?!

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:05.910
We got married.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:10.880
Eventually, after Youichi was born, Sora made a promise to me.

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:14.840
I'm going to grow a beautiful field of
 lavender on this mountainside, just for you!

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:19.330
Once it's finished, will you listen to me play my cello again, amongst the lavender?

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:21.680
And then...

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:27.990
Don't tell me...

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:34.040
Sora went up to Heaven and left me here alone.

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:38.540
So you never found out where the lavender field was?{Literally "what happened to it", but LATER CONTEXT etc.}

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:39.240
That's right.

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:42.580
Eventually Youichi got married,

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:44.540
and you were born.

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:47.040
But it's so strange.

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:54.210
I've grown so old, and yet, in my mind, 
Sora is still the same as he was back then.

00:10:55.110 --> 00:11:01.390
I suppose because he passed on so early, I 
still think of him as he was when we first met.

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:07.650
This was Grandpa's?

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:12.990
This is the last memento of his I have left.{'of his left' -> 'left of his'}

00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:15.410
Huh? What about the music box?

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:16.940
It's...

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:19.150
I...

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:20.600
What's the matter?

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:26.510
I loved that music box so much and always listened to it,

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:30.870
so Grandma gave it to me as a present,

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:35.340
but when we moved, it vanished from my luggage.

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:38.670
I'm so sorry, Grandma...

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:40.800
I've already forgiven you, you silly girl.

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:47.670
Besides, I'm sure that music box is helping to calm someone else's heart as it calmed mine.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:17.380
The summer sea, and not a Kumojacky or Kobraja in sight to ruin it.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:25.010
I'm going to make this a summer to remember!

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:26.850
Or I would, but...

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:29.970
this whole place is full of lovey-dovey couples!

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:33.620
This is all those accursed Precures' fault!

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:36.620
This time I'll defeat them, once and for all!

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:40.030
Sorry to bother you.

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:41.360
Mitsuru!

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.050
H-Hi there.

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:44.070
What's the matter?

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:48.780
W-Well, I have training this afternoon...

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:50.790
It won't be over till late, so...

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:51.790
Okay...

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:57.840
I mean, uh... I was running through the mountains recently, and I came across this lavender field.

00:12:57.840 --> 00:12:58.790
Huh?!

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:01.600
You like flowers, don't you?

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:03.380
I just wanted to tell you about it, so...

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:06.400
Is that the same lavender field?!

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:07.590
Sora's?!

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:12.890
Mitsuru, could you show us where it is?!

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:14.100
Sure!

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:17.860
It's just beyond the pass up ahead.

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.480
Are you all right?

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:22.900
Y-Yes.

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:25.720
Thank you, Itsuki!

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:28.990
I'm going on ahead!

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:30.950
Huh? Mitsuru!

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:36.850
Damn it all!

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:42.780
I thought the lavender field would be a
 good place to give her back the music box.

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:45.600
Can I really give it back to her, though?

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:46.890
What do we have here?

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:49.220
Whoa! A weirdo!

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:50.260
Hrm?

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:55.680
The flower of a troubled boy's
 heart. How beautifully it wilts!

00:13:56.300 --> 00:13:59.580
Flower of the Heart, come forth!

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:12.630
It's your cue, Desertrian!

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:18.580
Mitsuru?

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:20.540
Music box!

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:23.710
A Desertrian?!

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:25.340
It's Mitsuru!

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:27.670
They made him into a Deshertrian!

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:28.920
Huh?!

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:30.640
Please save Mitsuru!

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:31.600
Right!

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:43.270
Sheeds of the Precure, go forth!

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:47.920
Precure!

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.530
Open My Heart!

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:39.110
A lone flower, blooming from the earth!

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:44.310
Cure Blossom!

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:49.910
A lone flower, swaying in the sea breeze!

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:54.300
Cure Marine!

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:59.890
A lone flower, bathing in the Sun's rays!

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:03.850
Cure Sunshine!

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:10.450
HeartCatch Precure!

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:14.940
Music box!

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:18.030
Sunflower Protection!

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:24.250
Music box!

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:26.980
Whaaat?!

00:16:35.860 --> 00:16:38.310
Bombs away!{they're shouting "Tamaya" which is the name of an old famous fireworks company in old Japan. It's kind of customary to shout that whenever a firework goes up. I think this is sort of similarly cheeky but if you have a CUSTOMARY AMERICAN THING TO SHOUT DURING FIREWORKS that'd also be cool.} {We don't really have anything like that in Americaland, other than OOOH AHH WOW. So this works.}

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:47.400
I've had Hanasaki's music box all this time!

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:48.190
What?!

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:55.410
Huh... I feel sleepy...{Nobody interrupts my Metal Gear 1 reference. NOBODY.} {HNNNNNNNGGGGGGGGG.}

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:02.290
I saw something fall out of her car when she was moving, so I picked it up! {Added 'of.}

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:11.260
So that's what you ran after us!

00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:16.720
I chased after you to try to give it back, but I just couldn't catch up!

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:22.720
Hanasakiiiiiiiiii!

00:17:23.090 --> 00:17:24.430
So that's what happened!

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:26.690
Blossom!

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:39.490
Gather, Floral Power!

00:17:40.810 --> 00:17:43.380
Shiny Tambourine!

00:17:57.790 --> 00:17:59.680
Flowers, dance for me!

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:06.450
Precure Gold Forte Burst!

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:21.810
Hanasaki, I...

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:24.300
Mitsuru...

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:27.120
That's enough of the boring chit-chat.

00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:32.830
Fact is, as much as he sits there worrying, he 
didn't have the guts to give the music box back.

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:34.460
What a useless brat.

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:36.420
He's not useless!

00:18:36.890 --> 00:18:39.820
It's through those worries and 
uncertainties that people mature!

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:43.490
Using his heart and making it into a Desertrian is just cruel!

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:46.890
I've had it up to here with this!

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:57.550
Flowers, shine forth!

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:05.650
Precure Pink Forte Wave!

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:28.560
Hmph! I'll defeat you next time, just you watch!

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:31.600
You got the Flower of his Heart back!

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:33.480
Let'sh return him to normal!

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:45.410
You've finally come around?

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:47.050
Hanasaki...

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:54.300
So this must be the lavender field you were talking about, Mitsuru.

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:04.070
It's really pretty.

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:07.870
Hanasaki!

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:09.390
Here!

00:20:09.830 --> 00:20:13.350
You held onto it for me when it fell 
out of our car during the move, right? {Added 'of.'}

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:15.680
Huh? How did you know? {do -> did}

00:20:15.680 --> 00:20:17.860
Now, now, don't sweat the details.

00:20:18.680 --> 00:20:20.820
Mitsuru, thank you so much!

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:28.330
Ha.... Hana... saki...

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:29.740
Mitsuru?

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:32.390
I... I... I...

00:20:33.150 --> 00:20:34.250
I!

00:20:49.280 --> 00:20:52.380
Oh, right. What did you want to tell me just now?

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:54.640
It's nothing. Forget it.

